\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  My heart is struggling, searching,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 for the eternal peace.
\par But here, I'm perpetually
\par in the den of troubles.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In desperation I leave you,
\par and part with these problems.
\par To inherit eternal joy,
\par Oh Jesus, tarry not.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It's Thou that has redeemed me,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 from death and satan's grips.
\par Thou purchased me with Thy blood,
\par thou won victory for me.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Whatever threat can scare me
\par the enemy, his troop?
\par If I put all my hope in Thee,
\par I'll be a child of peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I don't enjoy worldly life,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 death is bitter for me.
\par If I live, I am for Thee,
\par and also die for Thee.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Life in Thee is good for me,
\par So receive my spirit.
\par Out of joy I give it out,
\par and it is gain for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  This carnal body will rot,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 and totally destroy.
\par That's why Christ will once again
\par transform it to be new.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par It will shine just as the sun
\par and get life for ever.
\par It will drink heavenly waters
\par filled with eternal life.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Life that is led in this world,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 is not what please my soul.
\par All its numerous glories
\par and even its beauties,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I deem them all vanity;
\par which will not last for long.
\par Rather the heavenly treasures,
\par that last for evermore.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  If I leave children orphans,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 they all bemoan in grief.
\par And it makes me feel for them,
\par with regard to their fate.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I should like to die with joy,
\par my hope is on the Lord.
\par He will be their Good Father,
\par He tends them forever.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  And now, Thou my Good Saviour,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 I'll be Thine evermore.
\par Oh grant me a peaceful death
\par so that angels of God,
\par take me to eternal life.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thy Divine property,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj Which through Thy suffering tortures,
\par and Thy death gained for me.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

